{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And the children of Israel came into the midst of the sea on dry ground.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): into the place where the sea had been they entered on dry ground." "<b>And by way of</b> the Midrash: if 'into the sea,' why 'on dry ground,' and if 'on dry ground,' why 'into the sea'? From this you learn that the sea did not split for them until they came into it up to their nostrils, and only afterward was it made dry ground for them. Rabbi Nehorai says: an Israelite woman would pass through with her child in her arms, and he would cry, and she would pluck an apple or a pomegranate from within the sea and give it to him, as it is said (Psalms 106): ״ויוליכם בתהומות כמדבר״ — 'and He led them through the depths as through a wilderness.' Just as in the wilderness they lacked nothing, as it is said (Deuteronomy 2): ״ארבעים שנה ה׳ אלהיך עמך לא חסרת דבר״ — 'these forty years HaShem your Elohim has been with you; you have lacked nothing' — so too in the depths they lacked nothing." "<b>And the waters were a wall for them on their right and on their left.</b> From this it follows that the path was in the middle, since the waters were on the right and on the left and above." "<b>And in the Midrash,</b> 'and the waters were a wall for them' — this is the Torah, compared to water, which they were destined to receive; it shielded them like a wall and destroyed the Egyptians. And this is why it is written חמה (ḥammah, 'wrath/heat'), missing the letter vav of חומה (ḥomah, 'wall'): for Israel it was חומה, a wall; for the Egyptians, חמה, wrath. 'On their right and on their left' — 'on their right,' in the merit of the Torah, as it is said (Deuteronomy 33): ״מימינו אש דת למו״; 'and on their left' — these are the tefillin, which are placed on the left."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:59:08.505228144Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}